  "prompt": "Recreate SCOUT's weather routing example: two routes across downtown Chicago, west and south of the Loop, from (41.896438, -87.659758) to (41.861649, -87.614034), starting at midnight on 6 July 2025, using SCOUT's routing model and its forecast with the default weather weights and one route per kind. Load downtown Chicago's roads from the Data Catalog, marked as roads so the map draws them, and find the fastest route and the weather-aware route once. Then compare them as two scenarios, \"Fastest route\" in blue (#4e79a7) and \"Weather-aware route\" in orange (#f28e2c), the first two colors of the Tableau10 scheme the map draws the routes in, the second a copy of the first: each keeps its route, as a band, and that route's metrics. Put both scenarios' routes in one layer, each named in a route column, and draw it over the roads on one map, colored by route with a categorical color scheme, so the map's own legend names the two routes; and chart the two routes' duration, distance, rain exposure and wind exposure on four Vega-Lite charts that compare the scenarios, one bar per scenario in its scenario's colour with its value above it. The routing model is not part of the standard node set, so whatever provides it needs installing first.",
  "context": null,
